<BlogLayout
  title="BOMA Area Measurement, Explained for People Who Sign Leases"
  description="What BOMA measurement standards actually measure, why rentable square footage differs from usable, and how a 3D scan gives you a defensible number for lease documentation."
  category="Guide"
  readTime="7 min"
>
  <p>Usable, rentable, load factor. Three terms decide what you actually pay on a commercial lease, and most tenants never learn how they differ until after they've signed. The space you walk around in and the space you pay rent on are two different numbers, measured under two different sets of rules. If you lease, own, or manage commercial space, it pays to understand those rules before the number lands in a contract.</p>

